# Datastar Cheatsheet

## 1. Four-Sentence Overview

- Datastar is "HTML + signals" sent from the server.
- The server owns permanent state and streams UI/Signal patches over SSE.
- The browser owns *ephemeral* state via lightweight, global signals.
- You wire the two together with declarative `data-*` attributes—no client components, no hydration.

## 2. Core Mental Model

### HTML is the contract

Element `id`s are API endpoints; the server sends fragments that morph into existing nodes.

### Two worlds, two responsibilities

- **Server**: business logic, DB access, template rendering, long-running flows.
- **Client**: last-millisecond UX—toggling, typing, progress bars—via signals.

### Continuous conversation

- Any user action can fire `@get/@post/…`.
- Response type decides the patch:
  - `text/event-stream` → stream of `patch-elements` + `patch-signals`
  - `text/html` → one-off DOM morph
  - `application/json` → signal merge

### State boundary

- Keep only what must survive a refresh on the server.
- Keep everything else (focus, open menus, form text) in signals.

## 3. Reactive Primitives

- `data-signals` - Mutable source of truth (`data-signals-count="0"` → `$count`).
- `data-computed` - Read-only derived signal (`data-computed-total="$price*$qty"`).
- `data-effect` - Runs expression now + on dependency change (`data-effect="$dirty && @post('/save')"`).
- `data-on-*` - Event handler (runs once per event; does *not* re-run on signal change).

Mnemonic: "S-C-E-E" → Signals, Computed, Effect, Event.

## 4. Attribute Cheat-Sheet (grouped)

### Bindings & Display

- `data-text` - Text content.
- `data-attr / data-attr-*` - Any attribute reactive (title, href, disabled…).
- `data-class / -*` - Toggle classes (`data-class-active="$sel===id"`).
- `data-style / -*` - Inline styles.
- `data-show` - `display:none` while expression is falsy.

### Two-way Form Helpers

- `data-bind / -*` - Value ↔ signal.
- `data-ref / -*` - Store DOM element in a signal (imperative escape hatch).

### State & Computation

- `data-signals / -*` - Declare or mutate signals.
- `data-computed / -*` - Derived, read-only signals.

### Effects / Lifecycle

- `data-effect` - Reactive side-effect.
- `data-on-load` - Fire once on process.
- `data-on-interval` - Polling timers.
- `data-on-intersect` - Viewport triggers.
- `data-on-signal-patch` - Global listener for incoming patches.

### Networking Indicators

- `data-indicator / -*` - Boolean "in-flight" flag tied to same element's request.

### Guard Rails

- `data-ignore` - Skip parsing.
- `data-ignore-morph` - Freeze subtree during DOM patches.
- `data-preserve-attr` - Keep selected attrs intact during morphs.

(Pro-only extras: persistence, query-string sync, RAF, resize, animate, etc.)

## 5. Backend Actions & the SSE Loop

Inside any expression you can call:

`@method('/url', options?)` → GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE

- All non-underscore (`_foo`) signals auto-sent (query or JSON body).
- `options.selector` - Serialize a form.
- `options.filterSignals` - `{include:/re/, exclude:/re/}`.
- Retry helpers (`retryInterval`, `retryMaxCount` …).

### Server responses:

1. `text/event-stream` → continuous patches, keeps HTTP conn open.
2. `text/html` → one fragment morph (target via `datastar-selector`).
3. `application/json` → merge into signals.
4. `text/javascript` → eval.

## 6. Common Recipes & SPA → Datastar Mapping

| Need | SPA way | Datastar idiom |
|------|---------|---------------|
| Local counter | useState | data-signals-count + data-text |
| Derived value | useMemo | data-computed-total="$a*$b" |
| Side-effect on change | useEffect | data-effect="$formDirty && @post('/autosave')" |
| Conditional section | `{show && …}` | data-show="$show" |
| "Click to Edit" | client state + API | Two server views keyed by same id; use @get/@put |
| Disabled while loading | isLoading state | data-indicator="isLoading" + data-attr-disabled="$isLoading" |

## 7. If you remember nothing else…

1. Server renders **HTML**; element `id`s are the API.
2. Client holds **signals** for moment-to-moment flair.
3. Four primitives (signals, computed, effect, events) cover 95% of interactivity.
4. `@get/@post` + SSE let the server patch both DOM and signals in real time.
5. Use `data-attr`, `data-class`, `data-style`, `data-show`, `data-text` to *reflect* signal changes onto the DOM—no extra JS required.

Now you can approach any UI problem the "Datastar-first" way:

- Ask "Is this state ephemeral?" → signal.
- Otherwise render it from the backend and, when it changes, stream a patch.